{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792893552,"nonce":"OQOjP0AREpi+Q6wzwK9XblesuQg=","message":"Likely cause: hot reload's object room. Caribou runs with reload on by default, and Ash's hlp_alloc_obj adds OBJECT_ROOM (ASH_RELOAD_ROOM, default 64 bytes) to every HOBJ instance, String, Array* and haxe.io.Bytes included; plain ash runs without reload. Probe (10k each of Bytes, 10-float arrays, small objects; major; dumpMemory): caribou room 64 marks 17.0 MB of lines in 523 blocks, caribou ASH_RELOAD_ROOM=0 13.8 MB in 425, ash 12.5 MB in 388. Raw live bytes fall 2.57 MB with the room off (64 bytes per instance). Before 9ca7955 Ash refused the room for programs whose plugin classes were laid out first, so whether ChimpMonk's runs had it is being checked (A/B with ASH_RELOAD_ROOM=0 on 1ca2bcc). Raised with ash-7d: room only for classes a reload can reshape, not std/runtime classes.","files":null}]}